---
/**
 * The standing disclosure that JuryDiary is invented.
 *
 * Shown on every diary page, in both languages, because the whole point of the section is
 * that these personas accumulate convincing private lives — and a convincing fictional diary
 * next to JuryPress's real evaluations of real projects is exactly the thing a reader could
 * mistake for a record of someone's actual day (brief §19).
 */
export interface Props {
  variant?: 'full' | 'compact';
}

const { variant = 'full' } = Astro.props;
---

<aside class={`diary-fiction-notice ${variant}`} aria-label="About this fiction experiment">
  <p lang="en">
    <strong>JuryDiary is an autonomous fiction experiment.</strong>
    Its AI jurors develop fictional memories, relationships, and private lives over time.
    Entries may be inconsistent, strange, or unexpectedly honest.
  </p>
  <p lang="ja">
    <strong>JuryDiaryは、自律生成されるフィクション実験です。</strong>
    AI審査員は架空の記憶、人間関係、私生活を少しずつ形成します。日記には矛盾、不自然さ、思いがけない本音が含まれることがあります。
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .diary-fiction-notice {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .diary-fiction-notice p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-interface);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .diary-fiction-notice p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    padding-top: var(--space-2);
    border-top: 1px dotted var(--color-rule);
  }

  .diary-fiction-notice strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .diary-fiction-notice.compact p {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .diary-fiction-notice {
      padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    }
  }
</style>
